# GITHUB-001: byte-exact fidelity for the release integrity chain.
#
# RELEASE_MANIFEST.json pins a SHA-256 and byte size for every tracked file,
# and scripts/verify_manifest.py fails the release gate on any mismatch.
# Git's default line-ending translation (core.autocrlf=true, the Git for
# Windows default) would rewrite CRLF files to LF on commit, changing their
# hashes and turning the first CI run red for a reason unrelated to code.
#
# '* -text' disables ALL line-ending translation, so what is committed is
# byte-identical to what was audited, on every platform and every clone.
#
# Verified safe: no shell script in this tree contains a carriage return,
# so nothing breaks under Linux/Oracle execution.
* -text
